<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine weekly official crop progress.</title>
<headline>Argentine weekly official crop progress.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine farmers had sown 76.5 percent of their intended 3.8 million hectares of 1996/97 maize by November 22, the Agriculture Secretariat said Thursday in its weekly crop report.</p>
<p>Sunflower sowing reached 82 percent of the 3.0 million hectares intended, which will be 11.9 percent down on last season. The area sown with soybeans reached 28.3 percent of the 6.3 million expected, an area 5.4 percent up on last year.</p>
<p>Wheat harvesting reached 11.6 percent of the 6.8 million hectares planned with average yields up at 17.1 qq/ha versus 15.3 last year and 14.2 the previous week.  </p>
<p>Intended total planting (thousands of hectares) and the percentage already sown (year-earlier in brackets). Harvest levels (thousands of hectares) and as a percentage of planted area, (year-earlier in brackets). Yield in quintals per hectare.</p>
<p> ..........Planting.............Harvest..................Yield</p>
<p> Wheat     6,867  100.0(100.0)   784.0   11.6   (n/a)   (17.1)</p>
<p> Maize     3,794   76.5 (70.9)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Soybeans    n/a    n/a  (n/a)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Sunflower 3,004   82.0 (68.0)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Sorghum     770   53.4 (41.6)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Cotton	989   39.9 (29.1)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
